+## September 13 — fleet cockpit correction and mobility authoring
+
+Source and workshop evidence: [reference fleet](REFERENCE_FLEET.md), [vehicle supply/ramp research](VEHICLE_REQUISITION_AND_RAMP_PLAN.md). Helicopter lower cockpit closed; wider three-across Humvee armored; 1.65 m thrust hoverboard and 18 m drone carrier modeled with shared-size detachable drones. Carrier pilot seat and native character scale retained. These are model/animation candidates, not accepted vehicle handling or live requisition. Current scout controller has no airtime. Future work should extend current movement/deployment owners. Facility models and stock integration remain proposed.
+
+
+### Fleet refinement — September 13
+
+[Reference fleet refinement](REFERENCE_FLEET.md): larger/deeper aircraft silhouettes and strategic ordnance, tank MG/recoil, shared presentation clips, mech park/stand, instanced cell missiles, nonmodal aim controls, armored motorcycle/grip pose, emblem placement ghost, and shared-geometry damaged/destroyed states. Workshop/model evidence only; many-vehicle mobile stress, live damage/boarding and vehicle handling remain separate gates. 40 native packages; source buffer sharing verified.
+
+### Fleet expansion — September 13
+
+Current [reference fleet](REFERENCE_FLEET.md): 36 intact / 23 damaged / 23 destroyed native models and 82 icons. Kestrel depth, distinct aircraft gun layouts, two-seat escort jet, standard helicopter/AA-tank stores, longer Humvee, cargo transport/ramp, carrier/hangar, runway and clipping-based fabrication preview. Saved camouflage and feet/metric toggle. Asset caps remain 32 draws / 4,948 triangles; 38 focused tests plus native reproduction and desktop/mobile workshop checks. Live ship/vehicle handling, boarding, collision and fabrication stock/spawn policy remain outside this authoring pass. No commit made.
+
+### Fleet expedition — September 13
+
+[Expedition authoring](FLEET_EXPEDITION.md) and [reference table](FLEET_REFERENCE_TABLE.md): twenty-troop aircraft; ten-troop armed hover transport; mobile, aircraft and gear printers; service rifle; cloning vat; warehouse; strategic launcher; nanite cloud/rat/hound/remote-mech forms; full-size bomber bomb bay; carrier aircraft storage, deck printer and below-deck service stations. Featured emblem panels and GPT Image Iron Jackal insignia. Proposed print times are labeled balance candidates, derived from model bounds. These are native model packages and workshop presentation, not live boarding, handling, inventory issuance or fabrication stock policy.
+
+### Nanite physical-form correction — 2026-09-13
+
+Replaced permanent fragmented rat/hound/remote-mech silhouettes with solid articulated robots, reconstruction seams and built-in Iron Jackal badges. Native triangle costs are 702 / 650 / 647; the 128-fragment effect is confined to assembly/dispersal. Nanites are excluded from fabrication payloads and proposed print times. Rebuilt 103 native variants and inventory icons. Native byte reproduction passed, focused expedition tests passed (7), and browser checks passed for solid endpoints, all form transitions, walking, material cleanup, mobile layout and printer/table exclusions. Production build verified; no native gameplay handling was added.
+
+### Predatory nanites and boarding handoff — 2026-09-13
+
+Rat and pit-bull hound now have driven cutting jaws, hook claws and articulated sensor tails. The remote robot is slimmer, retains red eyes/company badge, and has three reusable native wrist modules: claws, bullet gun and plasma cannon. Workshop previews cover forming/reforming hands (including mixed gun/plasma), slash/fire, lunge/bite, flight and dispersal defense. Rear transport entrances are framed, ramps meet ground, aircraft tail clears the boarding route, and a soldier can walk up the ramp to a seat. Other crewed vehicles expose entry-region previews. Unit purpose and branch handoff: FLEET_UNIT_HANDOFF.md. No live combat/boarding/flight rules were added.
+
+Verified: 49 focused tests; 106 native packages byte-reproduced and validated; 106 transparent inventory icons; browser action/boarding/mobile checks with no errors; occupied transport condition hide/restore; production build and matching final icon hashes.
